  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M.Kalianandi vs The State Of Tamil Nadu on 21 December, 2015 Author: D.Hariparanthaman Bench: D.Hariparanthaman Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated : 21.12.2015 Coram The Honourable Mr.Justice D.Hariparanthaman",
    "facts": "The post of Health Assistant was re-designated as Sanitary Officer in 1990. In 2010, the petitioner was appointed as Food Inspector in the Tirunelveli Municipal Corporation. 3.While so, Food Safety and Standards Authority Act, 2006 came into force in 2011. Thereafter, the petitioner was appointed as Food Safety Officer by the second respondent on 20.09.2011. He retired in the said post on 31.08.2014 on reaching the age of superannuation. 4.The grievance of the petitioner is that his benefits are not settled. According to him, the third respondent sent a letter dated 02.09.2014 to the second respondent stating that only respondents 1 and 2 have to settle the retirement benefits of the petitioner. But the second respondent wrote a letter dated 09.09.2014 to the third respondent to settle the retirement benefits of the petitioner.",
